---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Letters from '../components/Letters.astro';
import Photo from '../components/Photo.astro';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
const [profile]=await getCollection('profile');
const workLogos = { '/experience-logos/universiti-malaya.webp': '/experience-logos/um-club-supplied.png', '/experience-logos/pekom.webp': '/experience-logos/pekom-supplied.png', '/experience-logos/google-developers.webp': '/experience-logos/google-developers-supplied.png' };
---
<BaseLayout title="About"><nav class="about-tabs mono" aria-label="About sections"><a href="#bio">● Main bio</a><a href="#story">◆ Story</a><a href="#work">✦ Work</a></nav><div class="about-page"><h1 class="route-title"><Letters text="ABOUT" stagger={.06}/></h1><section id="bio"><h2 class="tape yellow">Main bio</h2><div class="bio-box" data-reveal><aside><Photo caption="2026"/><span class="sticker">TAN TED HANG</span></aside><p class="hand bio-lead">I’m Ted, a first-year Computer Science (Information Systems) student at Universiti Malaya. ✨ I’m interested in software development and full-stack work, practical AI applications, and human-centred product design. 🎨</p><p>I also work with photography, filmmaking, and video editing. Visual storytelling gives me another way to think about rhythm, attention, and how an idea reaches people.</p><p>I usually begin with questions. What is making this difficult? What does someone need to understand first? What should feel effortless, and where should the interface slow them down?</p><p class="highlight-note">{profile.data.forecast}</p><p class="bio-small">I’m still learning, and I want the portfolio to show that honestly. The work here is not a finished identity. It is a record of how I am becoming more deliberate about what I build and why.</p></div></section><section id="story" class="story-section"><h2 class="tape pink">Story</h2><div class="story-grid"><article data-drop><h3>Start with the why</h3><p>What is making this difficult? What does someone need to understand first? I begin with questions before treating technology as the answer.</p><p class="hand">questions before pixels.</p></article><article data-drop style="--delay:.1s"><h3>A creative practice</h3><p>Photography, filmmaking, video editing, and visual storytelling teach me to notice rhythm—what deserves attention, what should stay quiet, and how details become one experience.</p><p class="hand">notice the little things!</p></article><article data-drop style="--delay:.2s"><h3>Make it with the team</h3><p>In my university roles, I’m taking on responsibilities in publicity, public relations, and developer-community work, while learning how to move from an idea to working software.</p><p class="hand">us, not me.</p></article></div></section><section id="work" class="work-section"><h2 class="tape blue">Work</h2><div class="work-list">{profile.data.leadership.map(role=><article data-reveal><div class="work-identity"><img class="work-logo" src={workLogos[role.logo as keyof typeof workLogos] ?? role.logo} alt={`${role.organization} logo`} width="80" height="80" loading="lazy"/><div><h3>{role.role}</h3><p>{role.organization}</p></div></div><span class="mono">{role.period}</span></article>)}</div><div class="education-note" data-drop><span class="tape yellow">Education</span><h3>{profile.data.education.degree}</h3><p>{profile.data.education.institution} · {profile.data.education.period}</p><p>{profile.data.education.academicAchievements.join(' · ')}</p>{profile.data.awards.map(award=><p>{award.title}{award.year?` · ${award.year}`:''}</p>)}</div></section></div></BaseLayout>
